     "text": [
      "### LLM – Large Language Model\n",
      "\n",
      "A **Large Language Model (LLM)** is a type of artificial‑intelligence model that learns to understand, generate, and manipulate natural language text. The term “large” refers both to the sheer number of parameters (often billions to trillions) and to the massive datasets on which the model is trained. Here’s what you need to know:\n",
      "\n",
      "| Aspect | What it means |\n",
      "|--------|---------------|\n",
      "| **Architecture** | Most modern LLMs use the Transformer architecture (introduced in 2017). Key components: self‑attention, positional embeddings, multi‑head attention, feed‑forward layers. |\n",
      "| **Parameters** | Scale ranges from 1 B (Billion) to >500 B (for models like GPT‑4‑turbo) or even trillions (e.g., PaLM‑2). |\n",
      "| **Training data** | Hundreds of gigabytes to terabytes of text from books, Wikipedia, web crawls, code repositories, etc. |\n",
      "| **Pre‑training objective** | **Autoregressive** (predict next token, e.g., GPT) or **Masked Language Modeling** (predict missing tokens, e.g., BERT). |\n",
      "| **Fine‑tuning** | After pre‑training, the model can be adapted to specific tasks (translation, summarization, dialogue, etc.) via supervised or reinforcement learning. |\n",
      "| **Capabilities** | Text generation, question answering, summarization, translation, code generation, reasoning, and more. |\n",
      "| **Limitations** | - **Hallucination** (making up facts).<br>- **Bias & fairness** (reflects training data).<br>- **Computational cost** (training and inference).<br>- **Privacy concerns** (memorization of private data). |\n",
      "| **Common LLMs** | GPT‑4, GPT‑3.5, LLaMA‑2, PaLM‑2, Claude‑3, Gemini‑1, BLOOM, etc. |\n",
      "| **Ethics & Governance** | Responsible AI principles: transparency, bias mitigation, privacy safeguards, safety mechanisms, human oversight. |\n",
      "| **Industry impact** | • **Productivity**: Code assistants, customer support chatbots.<br>• **Creative**: Writing, music composition.<br>• **Research**: Summarizing literature, data analysis.<br>• **Education**: Tutoring, language learning. |\n",
      "| **Future trends** | • **Multimodal** (image + text, video).<br>- **Efficient architectures** (Sparse Transformers, LoRA, quantization).<br>- **Alignment & safety** (reinforcement learning from human feedback).<br>- **Domain‑specific models** (medical, legal). |\n",
      "\n",
      "---\n",
      "\n",
      "#### Quick FAQ\n",
      "\n",
      "| Question | Answer |\n",
      "|----------|--------|\n",
      "| *What does “large” really mean?* | It’s about having enough capacity to capture complex linguistic patterns, but also enough data to expose the model to diverse usage. |\n",
      "| *Do LLMs truly “understand”?* | They learn statistical patterns; they don’t possess consciousness or intentionality. |\n",
      "| *Can I train my own LLM?* | Yes, but it’s expensive. Small‑scale models (e.g., 125 M parameters) can be trained on consumer GPUs, while state‑of‑the‑art models need HPC clusters. |\n",
      "| *How do they stay up‑to‑date?* | By fine‑tuning on recent data or using continual learning. |\n",
      "| *Are they safe to use?* | With proper safeguards—content filters, bias monitoring, and human oversight—they can be used responsibly. |\n",
      "\n",
      "---\n",
      "\n",
      "#### TL;DR\n",
      "\n",
      "LLMs are big neural networks trained on massive text corpora, using the Transformer architecture to perform a wide range of language tasks. They power everything from chatbots to code generators, but require careful handling to mitigate bias, hallucination, and privacy risks.\n"
     ]
    }
   ],
   "source": [
    "\n",
    "from openai import OpenAI\n",
    "import os\n",
    "client = OpenAI(\n",
    "    api_key=os.environ.get(\"GROQ_API_KEY\"),\n",
    "    base_url=\"https://api.groq.com/openai/v1\",\n",
    ")\n",
    "\n",
    "response = client.responses.create(\n",
    "    input=\"llm\",\n",
    "    model=\"openai/gpt-oss-20b\",\n",
    ")\n",
    "print(response.output_text)\n"
   ]
  }
